===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|amphora||}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|ἀμφορεύς||vased shaped ornament with a narrow neck}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈæm.fə.ɹə/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|amphorae|amphoras}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A two [[handle]]d [[jar]] with a [[narrow]] [[neck]] that was used in [[ancient]] times to store or carry [[wine]] or [[oil]]s.
# One of various units for measuring liquid or volume during the Roman Empire, measuring between 18.5 and 39 [[litre]]s depending on the variant.
# An [[at sign]] (@).

